{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CROSS-TICKET NOTE from sibling d23e (deprecate REBAR_LLM_MODEL) — recorded as a COMMENT, deliberately not edited into this ticket's plan, because redesigning a production recovery path is the operator's call and not a side effect of a deprecation ticket.\n\nTHIS TICKET'S KILL SWITCH IS NOT BROKEN BY d23e. Verified before writing this: _deprecations._scheduled(...) sets permanent=False with remove_in=_MAJOR — it WARNS, it does not remove — and d23e's window explicitly keeps REBAR_LLM_MODEL functional. So 'REBAR_LLM_MODEL back to anthropic:...' still restores voting, before and after d23e lands. No safety change, and no action is required for this ticket to work.\n\nTHE DURABILITY PROBLEM IS REAL THOUGH. d23e lands BEFORE this ticket (S8 is blocked behind eb58, which cannot close until d23e does), so as written this ticket would CREATE a new infra/runbooks/ occurrence of a variable that was deprecated one ticket earlier, and put it in infra/compose/ too. That runbook then rots when the variable is removed at the next major — and a recovery runbook that has rotted is discovered at exactly the wrong moment.\n\nSUGGESTED, not imposed: express the kill switch in CLASS terms — configure the class slots, or set REBAR_LLM_<CLASS>_MODEL — which is a strictly equivalent one-line operator action with the same blast radius, and does not depend on a deprecated surface. If you prefer to keep REBAR_LLM_MODEL because it is the shortest possible action under incident pressure, that is a defensible choice; in that case the runbook should say explicitly that it uses a deprecated variable and name the class-based replacement alongside, so the entry does not silently rot.\n\nEither way the AC 'the kill-switch runbook entry exists under infra/runbooks/' stays satisfiable. d23e's docs criterion has been written so that nothing IT authors presents the deprecated variable as the recovery lever."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785584356320631001,"uuid":"c0840d28-69bf-47fc-b003-16f5d0c75848"}